cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "diff-negf: a benchmark-validated differentiable NEGF solver for inverse design of quantum transport"
abstract: >-
  An open, effective-mass one-dimensional coherent Non-Equilibrium Green's
  Function solver validated against two closed-form benchmarks and cross-checked
  against two algorithmically independent methods, together with a PyTorch
  differentiable implementation whose gradients are audited against central
  finite differences, a potential-to-transmission dataset with designated
  out-of-family test splits, a Fourier Neural Operator surrogate benchmarked
  against a parameter-matched multilayer perceptron, and an inverse-design
  protocol in which every proposed design is re-simulated and graded by the
  independently validated classical solver.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-23"
license: MIT
